## Loop usability finding (mandatory)
AWKWARD. claim TTL 30s requires a reliable heartbeat every ~20s. Observed twice this unit:
1. Prior CORD claim evaporated without ORCH spawn (heartbeat shell died) — named in unit brief.
2. ORCH heartbeat pid 38696 died mid-fanout; claims dropped to open until heartbeat restarted (pid 70446).
Doctrine now names "Claim TTL requires reliable heartbeat" in COMMS-ARCH. Proposed fix: raise work-claimed TTL to 90–120s OR provide a first-class `pheromone_heartbeat` / latch-integrated claim holder so agents need not keep a background shell alive; alternatively emit claim with ttl_s override when long critical sections are expected. Decay-as-coordination stays — the fix is reliability of the heartbeat carrier, not removing evaporation.

